    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d60">

                <pb facs="0118" n="852" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg852"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Thurston to Mr. Gresham.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hawaiian Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Washington D.
                                C.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1895-03-23"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">March 23,
                    1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In my communication to you under date of
                    January 20 last the statement was made that “the British commissioner in
                    Honolulu, Mr. Hawes, has called upon the Hawaiian Government to give him
                    assurances that no capital punishment will be inflicted upon the
                    insurrectionists.”</p>
                <p>Fuller information from my Government concerning such matter, received since the
                    date of such communication, is to the effect that the calls of Mr. Hawes on the
                    subject of capital punishment were unofficial, and I am instructed by my
                    Government to so inform you.</p>
                <p>With renewed assurances, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">L. A. Thurston.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
